1
00:00:06,725 --> 00:00:10,905
Last time, we asked: mould on bread, or yeast for making bread?

2
00:00:11,185 --> 00:00:12,445
Both are fungi!

3
00:00:12,715 --> 00:00:14,145
Which one is useful?

4
00:00:14,271 --> 00:00:15,451
Let's find out!

5
00:00:15,521 --> 00:00:16,801
One slice of bread.

6
00:00:16,961 --> 00:00:17,841
One bag.

7
00:00:17,971 --> 00:00:19,041
Ten days!

8
00:00:21,144 --> 00:00:22,454
You lock in first.

9
00:00:22,724 --> 00:00:24,534
One finger for every point.

10
00:00:24,824 --> 00:00:27,254
A little snail is hiding in this video.

11
00:00:27,514 --> 00:00:28,744
Can you spot it?

12
00:00:29,172 --> 00:00:30,562
Today you'll learn...

13
00:00:30,715 --> 00:00:32,495
How fungi get their food.

14
00:00:32,638 --> 00:00:34,108
How fungi spread.

15
00:00:34,259 --> 00:00:36,229
Useful or harmful fungi.

16
00:00:36,583 --> 00:00:37,523
Are you ready?

17
00:00:37,963 --> 00:00:38,733
Three!

18
00:00:39,113 --> 00:00:39,773
Two!

19
00:00:40,143 --> 00:00:40,793
One!

20
00:00:41,213 --> 00:00:41,933
Go!

21
00:00:42,687 --> 00:00:43,547
Day one.

22
00:00:43,846 --> 00:00:45,887
A slice of bread goes into a bag.

23
00:00:46,166 --> 00:00:47,157
We seal it.

24
00:00:47,427 --> 00:00:49,247
It stays shut for ten days.

25
00:00:57,501 --> 00:00:58,631
Ooh, fuzzy!

26
00:00:58,671 --> 00:01:00,691
Let me open the bag and sniff it!

27
00:01:00,896 --> 00:01:02,466
Something is not safe.

28
00:01:02,736 --> 00:01:04,916
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

29
00:01:05,196 --> 00:01:06,156
Hold on!

30
00:01:11,666 --> 00:01:12,796
Arms crossed?

31
00:01:13,067 --> 00:01:14,227
One finger up!

32
00:01:14,537 --> 00:01:16,276
Never touch or sniff mould.

33
00:01:16,556 --> 00:01:17,936
The bag stays shut.

34
00:01:18,289 --> 00:01:18,909
Oops.

35
00:01:19,229 --> 00:01:20,369
Eyes only!

36
00:01:20,865 --> 00:01:22,175
It is not dust.

37
00:01:22,445 --> 00:01:23,325
It grew!

38
00:01:23,750 --> 00:01:26,760
Bread mould is a fungus that grows on bread.

39
00:01:30,150 --> 00:01:31,370
One fungus.

40
00:01:31,810 --> 00:01:32,950
Many fungi.

41
00:01:34,565 --> 00:01:35,445
Round one.

42
00:01:35,765 --> 00:01:37,365
Living things need food.

43
00:01:37,625 --> 00:01:39,335
But nobody fed this mould!

44
00:01:39,615 --> 00:01:41,045
How does it get its food?

45
00:01:41,335 --> 00:01:42,885
One, it makes its own.

46
00:01:43,155 --> 00:01:44,505
Two, from the bread.

47
00:01:44,775 --> 00:01:46,535
Three, it needs no food.

48
00:01:46,825 --> 00:01:48,305
Show me with your fingers.

49
00:01:53,772 --> 00:01:54,752
Locked in!

50
00:01:54,880 --> 00:01:55,430
Three.

51
00:01:55,980 --> 00:01:57,270
Nobody fed it.

52
00:01:57,480 --> 00:01:59,260
Maybe it needs no food?

53
00:01:59,309 --> 00:01:59,919
Two!

54
00:02:00,089 --> 00:02:01,609
Living things need food.

55
00:02:01,739 --> 00:02:03,869
And the bread is the only food in there!

56
00:02:05,199 --> 00:02:06,149
Be a spore!

57
00:02:06,459 --> 00:02:07,439
Shrink down.

58
00:02:07,719 --> 00:02:08,649
Quietly.

59
00:02:10,934 --> 00:02:12,724
You are a spore of bread mould.

60
00:02:13,164 --> 00:02:14,934
You float in the kitchen air.

61
00:02:15,443 --> 00:02:17,263
You land on a slice of bread.

62
00:02:17,772 --> 00:02:19,122
The bag closes.

63
00:02:19,542 --> 00:02:21,092
You are already inside!

64
00:02:21,685 --> 00:02:23,875
You grow thin threads into the bread.

65
00:02:24,461 --> 00:02:26,091
You make a substance.

66
00:02:26,511 --> 00:02:30,091
It breaks the bread down into simpler substances.

67
00:02:30,686 --> 00:02:32,506
You absorb them as food.

68
00:02:33,165 --> 00:02:36,295
You grow into a fuzzy patch, and make new spores.

69
00:02:38,515 --> 00:02:39,825
The answer is two.

70
00:02:40,095 --> 00:02:41,145
From the bread!

71
00:02:41,644 --> 00:02:42,804
Say it with me!

72
00:02:43,512 --> 00:02:46,582
Fungi are living things that do not make their own food.

73
00:02:46,802 --> 00:02:48,722
Fungi grow on another object.

74
00:02:48,772 --> 00:02:52,572
They produce a substance to break down the other object into simpler

75
00:02:52,322 --> 00:02:55,112
substances and absorb them as food.

76
00:03:00,184 --> 00:03:01,214
Two fingers?

77
00:03:01,484 --> 00:03:02,704
One finger up!

78
00:03:03,127 --> 00:03:04,967
A mushroom is a fungus too.

79
00:03:05,237 --> 00:03:06,167
The cap.

80
00:03:06,607 --> 00:03:07,637
The stalk.

81
00:03:08,067 --> 00:03:09,917
And under the cap, the gills.

82
00:03:09,973 --> 00:03:10,883
Nice cap!

83
00:03:10,973 --> 00:03:12,303
Can I try it on?

84
00:03:12,727 --> 00:03:16,067
Mushrooms have spores that are found in gills under the cap.

85
00:03:16,347 --> 00:03:19,277
When the wind blows, the spores are dispersed.

86
00:03:19,788 --> 00:03:21,078
Say it with me!

87
00:03:21,793 --> 00:03:24,843
Fungi can reproduce very quickly through spores.

88
00:03:30,807 --> 00:03:32,957
Now, the question from last time!

89
00:03:33,247 --> 00:03:34,837
Which fungus is useful?

90
00:03:35,157 --> 00:03:36,097
One, mould.

91
00:03:36,377 --> 00:03:37,367
Two, yeast.

92
00:03:37,657 --> 00:03:38,967
Show me your fingers!

93
00:03:42,436 --> 00:03:43,416
Locked in!

94
00:03:43,579 --> 00:03:44,333
Two!

95
00:03:44,573 --> 00:03:45,343
Yeast!

96
00:03:45,423 --> 00:03:46,883
It makes the dough rise.

97
00:03:46,931 --> 00:03:47,701
Yes!

98
00:03:48,031 --> 00:03:48,831
Yeast.

99
00:03:49,193 --> 00:03:51,333
So are all the other fungi harmful?

100
00:03:51,681 --> 00:03:55,291
There are some fungi that are useful, while others are harmful to

101
00:03:55,041 --> 00:03:55,601
us.

102
00:03:55,962 --> 00:03:59,532
Edible mushrooms are useful since they are food for us.

103
00:03:59,912 --> 00:04:01,782
Never pick wild mushrooms!

104
00:04:02,141 --> 00:04:07,131
Yeast is another useful fungus as it is commonly used in baking

105
00:04:06,881 --> 00:04:09,131
bread to make the dough rise.

106
00:04:11,715 --> 00:04:14,245
Tempeh is made with a useful fungus.

107
00:04:15,590 --> 00:04:18,600
Bread mould is an example of harmful fungi.

108
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:21,750
Eating mouldy bread can cause us to fall sick.

109
00:04:21,964 --> 00:04:22,994
Two fingers?

110
00:04:23,264 --> 00:04:24,484
One finger up!

111
00:04:24,907 --> 00:04:26,367
Show me your score hand!

112
00:04:26,657 --> 00:04:27,687
More than two?

113
00:04:27,967 --> 00:04:29,337
You beat the Buddies.

114
00:04:29,637 --> 00:04:30,697
Three fingers?

115
00:04:30,977 --> 00:04:31,987
High five!

116
00:04:32,634 --> 00:04:34,064
Did you spot the snail?

117
00:04:34,354 --> 00:04:35,604
It was on the window!

118
00:04:35,904 --> 00:04:37,444
Is a snail a fungus?

119
00:04:37,714 --> 00:04:39,014
Tell someone at home.

120
00:04:39,742 --> 00:04:41,942
Let's read today's key words together!

121
00:04:42,232 --> 00:04:42,992
Ready?

122
00:04:43,279 --> 00:04:44,299
Bread mould.

123
00:04:45,734 --> 00:04:46,654
Absorb.

124
00:04:48,110 --> 00:04:48,990
Spores.

125
00:04:50,473 --> 00:04:51,165
Yeast.

126
00:04:52,596 --> 00:04:53,536
Well done!

127
00:04:54,633 --> 00:04:55,573
Day ten.

128
00:04:55,853 --> 00:04:58,223
The bag goes into the bin, still shut.

129
00:04:58,493 --> 00:04:59,933
Then we wash our hands.

130
00:05:00,068 --> 00:05:01,498
But they look clean!

131
00:05:01,628 --> 00:05:02,908
So what is on them?

132
00:05:03,208 --> 00:05:04,788
Find out in Part Two!

133
00:05:06,151 --> 00:05:07,255
Say it with us!

134
00:05:08,056 --> 00:05:08,806
Ready?

135
00:05:08,929 --> 00:05:09,589
One!

136
00:05:09,929 --> 00:05:10,629
two!

137
00:05:10,934 --> 00:05:12,109
Now you know!
